532 - Day by Day
 / 
Key: D
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 532
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[D]Day by day, and with each passing [Em]moment,
Strength I [A]find to meet my trials [D]here;
[D]Trusting in my Father's wise be[Em]stowment,
I've no [A]cause for worry or for [D]fear.
[D]He, whose heart is kind beyond all [Em]measure,
Gives unto each [A]day what He deems [D]best,
Loving[Bm]ly its [D7]part of pain and [Em]pleasure,
[E]Mingling [A]toil with peace and [D]rest.

Verse 2:
[D]Every day, the Lord [Em]Himself is near me
[A]With a special [D]mercy for each hour;
[D]All my cares He fain [Em]would bear, and cheer me,
[A]He whose name [D]is Counselor and power.
[D]The protection of [Em]His child and treasure
[A]Is a charge that [D]on Himself He laid;
[Bm]As your days, [D7]your strength shall [Em]be in measure,
[E]This the [A]pledge to [D]me He made.

Verse 3:
[D]Help me then [Em]in every tribulation
[A]So to trust [D]Thy promises, O Lord,
[D]That I lose [Em]not faith's sweet consolation
[A]Offered me within [D]Thy holy Word.
[D]Help me, Lord, when [Em]toil and trouble meeting,
[A]E'er to take, as [D]from a father's hand,
[Bm]One by [D7]one, the days, [Em]the moments fleeting,
[E]Till I [A]reach the [D]promised land.
